This program is a Python login system.
The variable "login" is used to repeat the program.

The program asks the user for a username and a correo.
The variable "correo" is the email entered by the user.

The program checks the correo.
It verifies if the correo has "@" and ".".
It also checks if the correo starts with invalid characters like "@" or ".".
The program also checks if the correo has enough characters.

Now the program is validating the correo format.

Then the program asks the user for a password.
The variable "user_password" is the password of the user.

The program checks if the password has at least eight characters.
It also verifies if the password contains numbers, uppercase letters, and special characters.

Now the system is analyzing each character of the password.

Finally, the program prints messages depending on the result.
If the password meets the conditions, the user can enter the system.
If the password is not valid, the program shows an error message and asks the user to try again.
